<newsitem itemid="652615" id="root" date="1997-06-11" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Foschini yr shr falls sharply.</title>
<headline>Foschini yr shr falls sharply.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - attrib		  77.9	  vs 107.4</p>
<p>Analysts polled by Reuters forecast earnings per share falling to between 93.1 and 105.0 cents with consensus at 98.1.</p>
<p>The group said it would award capitalisation shares.  </p>
<p>    Attrib income	   165.1	 vs 227.5</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   245.7	 vs 346.0</p>
<p>    Tax			 78.9	  vs 120.0</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   54.4	  vs 58.2</p>
<p>    Turnover		  2,256.5     vs 2,183.3</p>
<p>    Share of associates'  1.7 loss    vs 1.5 gain</p>
<p>Full name: Foschini Ltd  </p>
<p>Directors said the capitalisation shares would be issued to holders registered on June 27 in the ratio of three new fully paid ordinary shares for every 100 ordinary shares held and would be posted on July 4.</p>
<p>-- Cape Twon newsroom +27 21 25 2238</p>
</text>
